  "method": "Dominica, whole island, with the Soufrière-Scotts Head Marine Reserve (SSMR) in the southwest and the Cabrits/Douglas Bay area in the north. The SSMR's own Dive Sites in the SSMR page (ssmrdominica.com), published by the reserve, is the official list and counts as one; it gives no coordinates and no numbered mooring list (the Fisheries Division publishes none online, and the UNESCO tentative-list text only names the headline sites). Operator lists read: Dive Dominica (Castle Comfort) and Cabrits Dive Center (Portsmouth). Nature Island Dive (Soufrière), SALT Dominica (Toucari) and Fort Young Dive publish no site list (images, rates or sales copy only, or the domain is dead or blocked), and East Carib Dive has closed, so they add nothing. A site is counted when named on at least two independent lists; sites on one list stay as excluded. Name merges: L'Abym is also La Sourcière (Witches Point); Scotts Head Pinnacle includes Swiss Cheese, where the dive begins; Dive Dominica's Coral Gardens North (Dangleben's North) is read as the Coral Gardens inshore of Dangleben's Pinnacles, which is doubtful, so Dangleben's Pinnacles itself stays on the reserve list only. Every northern site is on the Cabrits Dive Center list alone, so the north is largely excluded for lack of a second independent list (blogs such as a-virtual-dominica corroborate them but cannot count). Everything listed is within recreational depth. Counted 2026-10-14.",
